{
  "id": "i02-l06",
  "unit": "i02-and-then",
  "title": "Right? Tags and particles",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Small words change the tone:\n\n- **…, তাই না?** 'isn't it? / right?' asks for agreement: **আজ খুব গরম, তাই না?**\n- **…, না?** is the short, casual tag: **তুমি আসবে, না?**\n- **তো** adds 'but, after all, you know': **আমি তো বলেছি!** 'But I told you!'\n- **নাকি** has two jobs. Between options it is 'or': **চা নাকি পানি?** In a statement it means 'apparently, I hear': **রাফি নাকি অসুস্থ** 'I hear Rafi is ill.'\n\n**আরে!** 'hey!, oh!' shows surprise. **দেখা হল** '(we) met'.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "tai-na",
      "bn": "তাই না",
      "tr": "tai na",
      "en": "isn't it? / right?"
    },
    {
      "id": "to",
      "bn": "তো",
      "tr": "to",
      "en": "(emphatic particle)"
    },
    {
      "id": "naki",
      "bn": "নাকি",
      "tr": "naki",
      "en": "apparently; or",
      "notes": "Between options: 'or' (চা নাকি পানি?). In a statement: 'I hear, apparently'."
    },
    {
      "id": "na-tag",
      "bn": "না",
      "tr": "na",
      "en": "right? (tag)",
      "notes": "Same spelling as না 'no, not' (U1); at the end of a sentence it asks for agreement."
    },
